r that Candidate C demonstrates strong teamwork/communication skills and a commitment to professional growth, would shift my preference.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}", "thoughts": "We have now info from Agent 1 about stress handling for A (none) and D (some). Now we need to produce our public message with provisional preference.\n\nWe need to consider all candidates with info we have.\n\nOur own info (from initial list) includes:\n\nCandidate A: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, relatively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, keeps calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nWe also have from Agent 1: D's stress handling as above.\n\nNow evaluate for long-distance pilot: need reliability, technical competence, calm under pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nLet's assess each:\n\nA: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Weakness: show-off, not open to new ideas. No explicit stress handling. Leadership good but maybe overconfidence. Lack of openness could affect learning. No mention of teamwork/communication. So mixed.\n\nB: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (good), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (tech). Weakness: weak memory for numbers (could be issue for calculations), makes nasty remarks (teamwork problem). So strong on stress and technical, but poor interpersonal.\n\nC: quick correct decisions (decision-making), keeps calm in crisis (calmness), understands complicated tech (technical), but difficulty communicating ideas (teamwork), egocentric (team), not willing to further education (development). So strong decision and calm, weak teamwork and development.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously (reliability), but hot temper (calmness), know-it-all (teamwork). So strong problem solving, but temperament issues.\n\nWe need to weigh. For long-distance flights, calmness under pressure and teamwork are crucial. B handles stress well but nasty remarks could be dangerous. C keeps calm and makes quick decisions, but communication issues could be problematic. D problem solving but hot temper could be risky. A lacks stress info, but good anticipation and leadership, but show-off and not open to new ideas.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? Possibly Candidate C because calmness, quick decisions, technical understanding, but communication issues are serious. However, long-distance flights require crew coordination; difficulty communicating could be fatal. B's nasty remarks also harmful. D's hot temper also harmful. A's lack of stress handling unknown, but leadership and anticipation could compensate? But not open to new ideas could hinder learning.\n\nWe might be undecided, but need provisional preference. Perhaps Candidate C is strongest in core pilot skills (decision, calm, technical) though teamwork is a concern. Could be mitigated with training. B's stress handling is good but interpersonal issues severe. D's hot temper also severe. A's unknown stress handling is a big unknown.\n\nThus provisional preference: Candidate C.\n\nWe should note uncertainty about communication and willingness to develop. What would change? Evidence of strong teamwork or willingness to improve, or evidence that A handles stress well, or that D's temper is manageable.\n\nNow produce output."}
